OL,3,AExpect fewer frosts and more hot days
OL,4,Aas UK seasons shift, says Met Office
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe UK's seasons are changing, with
OL,7,Ffewer winter frosts and more hot summer
OL,8,Fdays, according to new analysis from
OL,9,Fthe Met Office.
OL,11,FAcross the UK, the number of winter
OL,12,Fdays with an air frost ` when the air
OL,13,Ftemperature falls to 0C or below ` was
OL,14,Faround a quarter lower in the decade to
OL,15,F2025 than during the period from 1961
OL,16,Fto 1990.
OL,18,FIn southern England, the reduction was
OL,19,Faround a third while the average number
OL,20,Fof UK summer days reaching 25C has more
OL,21,Fthan doubled.
OL,23,APub: 26-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/39
